# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0013606> (Hermansky-Pudlak syndrome 9)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22461475") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26575419") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29054114") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40028/") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7437-8060") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0013606> "Any Hermansky-Pudlak syndrome in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the BLOC1S6 gene, resulting in defective melanosomes and absence of platelet dense granules. The phenotype includes oculocutaneous/ocular albinism with nystagmus and reduced visual acuity and a bleeding tendency. Distinguishing features can include leukopenia with recurrent infections and thrombocytopenia in some patients.")
